WHY THE METHODOLOGY IS OPENLY LICENSED

A benchmark that cannot be checked is not a benchmark. IOSCO transparency and the
project's own governance both require the methodology to be public, so licensing
it openly costs nothing and makes the transparency real rather than nominal: a
reader may reproduce it, quote it at length, translate it, or publish a critique
that includes it.

Attribution is the one condition, and it is the point. The methodology and the
values computed under it are only meaningful when it is clear who computed them
and under which published version. That correspondence is protected by the
trademark, not by this licence — see NOTICE.
